Construction notes, all deliberate.

1. The hash is recorded HERE rather than inside the plan, because writing
   a document's hash into that document changes the hash. Same two-tier
   pattern used for the paper's anchored artifacts: payload in one file,
   attestation in another.

2. The plan contains NO fields to be filled in later. Execution state —
   versions pinned, hours, results, publication dates — lives in
   EXECUTION-LOG.md, which is mutable by design.

3. See section 11 of the plan for what the "review" of this document
   actually was: two rounds of adversarial review by a separate AI model
   instance. NOT human expert review, NOT peer review, and conferring no
   warrant. An earlier draft described it as "external specialist review,"
   which implied a human credential that does not exist. That wording was
   corrected before publication.

